## Overview

This is the foundation sensor set for Droid Works USA.

In Lesson Set 01 you will build and test the individual sensor modules one at a time, give each physical device a persistent identity, discover the devices over USB, convert their raw serial output into clean ROS 2 topics, fuse related sensors, and create simple state nodes that the rest of the system can listen to.

The goal is not simply to make four sensors work.

The goal is to build a **modular sensor layer** that can be expanded later without forcing the rest of the system to know which physical USB port or sensor is being used.

By the end of this set you will have:

* Working Arduino sensor modules and sketches
* Persistent EEPROM device identities
* USB device discovery using VID/PID
* Device identification using EEPROM metadata
* ROS 2 entry nodes for each individual sensor
* A PIR motion sensor pipeline
* An RCWL motion sensor pipeline
* A motion fusion node combining PIR and RCWL
* An Ultrasonic distance sensor pipeline
* A Time-of-Flight distance sensor pipeline
* A distance fusion node combining Ultrasonic and ToF
* Separate motion and distance state nodes

These components form the basic sensor layer used by the rest of the Droid Works USA system.

